WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.830
Hey Team it’s Charlie and this week’s
episode of Doctor Who did an amazing job of

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.170
tying back into the idea of changing mistakes
of the past.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:14.400
Peter Capaldi himself described it as a combination
of Ocean’s Eleven and 2001 Space Odyssey.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.840
I would also add the Wizard of OZ to that.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.000
So let’s do top 5 moments, easter eggs and
then the review.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.590
And quick reminder, the weekly giveaway is
open again.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.369
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:28.230
Careful for spoilers from the episode.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.580
I’ll wait just a sec...okay.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.010
Here are my top 5 moments.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.429
Number 5 - The Bank of Karabraxos

00:00:36.429 --> 00:00:40.789
If this was supposed to be a little bit Ocean’s
Eleven, I’m guessing Karabraxos is the Bellagio

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:41.789
Hotel.

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:46.140
This was probably one of the most well developed
new locations in series 8.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.480
Because of the macguffin of the Heist they
were able to describe every detail of the

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.510
planet and the bank down to the last spec
of dust.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.030
I wish we could get a big episode like that
inside the TARDIS.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.479
Even Journey to the Center of The TARDIS in
series 7 didn’t explain the interior workings

00:00:59.479 --> 00:01:03.679
of the TARDIS as well as Time Heist explained
the Bank of Karabraxos.

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:07.579
The culture of the bank was just as interesting.

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:10.469
Did you catch when they killed the Red Shirt
at the beginning?

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:13.590
Miss Delphox said they were going to terminate
his account, meaning the bank would seize

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.789
his assets and they’d throw his family in
jail.

00:01:16.789 --> 00:01:18.390
That seems a bit harsh.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:21.200
Maybe Moffat hates white collar criminals.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.080
It also explains how Miss Karabraxos could
become the wealthiest person in the Universe.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.119
If she just kept terminating accounts and
taking people’s fortunes.

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:33.369
I liked the idea of the architect even though
the reveal was kind of obvious.

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:38.369
The other direction I thought they could have
gone would have been for the Doctor himself

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:39.369
to be the architect.

00:01:39.369 --> 00:01:44.180
And had his mind wiped.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.369
That would have messed the whole plot up.

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:50.930
And they already did the multiple mind wipes
joke with Strax during the 2012 Christmas

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.509
Special.

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:59.319
The solar storm that destroyed the planet
was the same type of storm that destroyed

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.319
all the gangers during Rebel Flesh and Almost
People.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.229
Not the same storm, but the same type of storm.

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:04.579
Number 4 - The New Monster The Teller

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:06.859
Technically not a monster as we learned.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:15.390
But as far as the episode explained it’s
psychic and prevents people for stealing or

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.130
cheating the bank.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:23.100
I lot of you told me on twitter it reminded
you of the Minotaur from God Complex.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.830
In both cases the story was about turning
your own thoughts against you.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:36.940
There was a nice moment when it was scanning
the Doctor’s Brain that I wondered if we’d

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.570
get some big clue about Missy.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:44.490
I just ended up being the Madam Karabraxos
reveal but it did make us think about the

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.490
TARDIS phone again.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.070
I’ll talk more about the phone during my
review.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:52.650
Because the Doctor did way to many mimed phone
calls at people for it to be a throwaway joke.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.340
I would have liked to learn a little more
about the Teller creatures but now that they’re

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.690
canon, they can always come back.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:03.190
I feel like Moffat wouldn’t create something
with those kind of powers if he didn’t intend

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:06.740
for the Doctor to ask a favor of them in exchange
for saving their lives.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.200
Back in Deep Breath he said he remembered
his face but he didn’t remember why he picked

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.200
it.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.750
It’s possible the teller’s could deep
scan his brain to find out or give him a clue.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.430
Number 3 - The Doctor’s Toys offer some
clues about Missy

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:24.341
I don’t know if the Dimensional Shift Bomb
was timelord technology but he had it on him

00:03:24.341 --> 00:03:26.500
and I don’t think anyone else gave it to
him.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.750
And then there was the quick return buttons
he handed out.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:33.330
As for the Bomb, He said instead of exploding
it sends particles to another plane of existence.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:38.230
He didn’t say which plane or if it was like
E-Space or a pocket universe.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.250
The quick return capsules were tied to the
TARDIS, so I’m guessing those were timelord

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.250
technology.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:46.690
If Missy had her own TARDIS, that could be
how she’s snagging people.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:52.100
It’s still a little soon to tell.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:04:00.370
I always love new gadgets.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.810
Like David Tennant’s machine that goes Ding
in the 50th.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:06.650
It makes it feel like the Doctor’s suits
also operate like the TARDIS and are bigger

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:07.650
on the inside.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.420
Like they have infinite storage space in their
pockets.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.870
Number 2 - The Private Vault

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:15.360
I’m going to have to re-watch this a couple
more times to see but I feel like there are

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.260
a lot of visual easter eggs for other bits
of Doctor Who history.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:23.710
The egyptian symbols made me think of Pyramids
of Mars and the upcoming Mummy on the Orient

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.370
Express episode.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:30.530
A lot of times set designers will insert their
own easter eggs when putting props in the

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:31.530
backgrounds of shots.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:36.750
Things that aren’t really in camera focus,
but if you were on the set you’d be able

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.770
to see really clearly.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:41.780
Doctor Who recycles a lot of their props too,
so sometimes when you see familiar things

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.780
it’s both them just being practical and
saving money and the set designer picking

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:47.670
things because they have some special significance.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.370
Mark Gatiss explained that sometimes it just
ends up being a coincidence.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.590
He was talking about his own writing, but
I like to think that people who are not Moffat

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.010
on the crew try to work in things they think
the fandom will pick up on.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:58.610
So let me know if you saw anything in the
vault at the end that reminded you of stuff

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.610
from previous episodes.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:05.600
and my Number 1 thing - Keeley Hawes new Villain
Madam Karabraxos and Miss Delphox

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.680
She is now the second biggest person this
season to play multiple roles in the same

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:10.680
episode.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.630
Clara is the impossible girl, but I’m not
counting her.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:18.760
Samuel Anderson played two different versions
of his character and now Keeley Hawes.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:22.770
I wonder if the trend will continue.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:39.370
I loved her character but I feel like she
got short changed a little.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:44.150
Both versions of her character, Miss Karabraxos
and the clone Miss Delphox were really interesting.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:48.410
And you could tell the clone had a life of
her own.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.450
She was kind of like one of the gangers.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:54.700
Add to that she was going to be thrown in
the incinerator just like the gangers getting

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.700
dumped in acid.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.280
It’s important to remember that Madame Karabraxos
didn’t die at the end.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:02.270
She’s still out there somewhere so Keeley
Hawes could always come back to reprise the

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:03.270
character.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.520
I think one of my favorite things about the
big reveal was the way her story mirrored

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:07.520
the doctor’s.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.990
And with her hating herself, all the deep
regrets about changing the past.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:15.220
It’s what’s happening with The Doctor
right now.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.870
It was a great way to tie the plot of the
episode to one of the big themes of series

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:20.870
8.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:24.230
So my big questions for you guys is, what
was your favorite moment and do you think

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:31.450
we’ll see the Teller creatures or Keeley
Hawes again?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:36.200
I already mentioned a lot of the references
I spotted like the gangers, the vault and

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.200
the tardis phone.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:41.210
But here are all the criminals that popped
up on the screen.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:44.420
There was the Terileptil, which was mentioned
during the Christmas Special.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.630
The Slitheen also mentioned in the christmas
special.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.270
A Sensorite from the Sensorites.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:54.290
That was the seventh story from doctor who
season 1.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.940
Absalom Daak from the comics.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:07:01.440
Then there were a couple from the sarah jane
adventures including Androvax, The Trickster

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:05.760
and Captain John Hart from Torchwood

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:10.050
I feel like they were the biggest reference,
but if you saw any other big ones in the episode

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:11.710
just write them in the comments.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:16.360
Overall I gave this episode a B, it was a
lot of fun but I felt like the plot dissolved

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:19.250
after they rescued the doctor and went down
to the vault.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.290
Keeley Hawes was very interesting, she’s
a great actress.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.419
But I feel like she didn’t get enough time
to develop her characters.

00:07:25.419 --> 00:07:32.260
This whole thing with one actor playing multiple
versions of themselves seems very suspicious.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.220
The supporting guest cast were a lot of fun.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:39.540
I always wonder what and who Moffat plans
on bringing back at the end of each series.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.820
Psi’s moment with Clara where he explains
deleting his family from his brain felt like

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.110
setup for Clara in a later episode.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.300
I feel like the only problem I had with the
story was that the explanation was a little

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.300
too simple in the end.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.430
There was all this build up for the first
half of the episode and wizard of oz style,

00:07:52.430 --> 00:08:01.100
the curtain is thrown back and it’s a frail
dying person behind it all.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:07.460
I think we can blame that on the episode this
year being less serialized.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:12.900
As a result they have to completely set everything
up and resolve it in 50 minutes, so if it

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.620
feels like it was too easy for them to rob
the bank.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:24.290
That’s why, they had to do Ocean’s Eleven,
a two plus hour movie, in under 50 minutes.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:36.999
Actually they did the Ocean’s Eleven part
in under 40 minutes or so, the last ten was

00:08:36.999 --> 00:08:39.419
wizard of oz.

00:08:39.419 --> 00:08:44.399
It was still a lot of fun but I really do
like serialized stories more.

00:08:44.399 --> 00:08:47.470
It just allows them to make more complex storylines.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.689
I understand why they’re not doing that.

00:08:49.689 --> 00:08:52.529
They just want to make it easier for new viewers
to follow.

00:08:52.529 --> 00:08:54.339
Next week looks like a lot fun.

00:08:54.339 --> 00:08:56.920
The Doctor will be play acting headmaster
at Coal Hill.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:00.570
My next video is going to be my bonus story
for the christmas special this year.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.920
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.540
They just announced a bunch of guest actors.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.850
so I’ll try to post that in 5 or 6 hours.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:10.459
Don’t forget about the giveaway, I’ll
announce the winner in my Q&amp;A on Sunday

00:09:10.459 --> 00:09:12.720
Right now click here for the bonus video.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.290
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.199
and click here for the Q&amp;A.

00:09:17.199 --> 00:09:20.769
Thanks for watching, everybody high five and
we’ll meet up again in a couple hours to

00:09:20.769 --> 00:09:21.709
talk about the christmas special!

